d0=A.aS(b9,"8-2",A.a([c6,c5,c3,c9,A.d(h9,0,A.a([0,1,3],p),"Visible copies and discards by the players you fear both cut the chance that the tile completes their hand.",d0,h9,"Which of these make a tile safer to discard?",h9,B.B),A.d(h9,0,h9,"Absolute safety lasts only until the opponent draws again, while four visible copies means no fifth copy exists to win on.",B.k,B.SP,"Match each situation to how safe that tile is against the player you fear.",h9,B.C),A.d(h9,0,h9,"There are only four copies of any tile, so once all four are visible nobody can complete a pair, pong or wait with it.",A.a(["No opponent can hold or wait on a fifth copy","It must be an honour tile","Every player has already thrown it","It must be a terminal tile"],n7),h9,"Why is a tile with all four copies visible completely safe to discard?",h9,B.h),A.d(h9,2,h9,"A fresh middle tile is the classic danger tile, because it connects to many sequences and all four copies are still live.",A.a(["The threatening opponent discarded it this rotation","All four copies are visible","It is a fresh middle tile nobody has played","Two opponents have already thrown it away"],n7),h9,"Which of these is NOT a reason for a tile to be safe?",h9,B.h),A.d(A.a(["0","zero","none","no copies"],n7),0,h9,"All four copies are accounted for, so no opponent can be waiting on a tile that no longer exists in play.",B.k,h9,"You can see all four copies of {{p6}} on the table. How many copies could an opponent still be waiting on?",h9,B.v)],o),l5,"Minimizing deal-in risk","Safe Tile Theory")
c9=A.a([A.x(h8,"Sometimes the best play is NOT to win! Defensive play (\u6253\u9632\u5b88) means prioritizing safe discards over building your hand.",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"When to play defensively: Your hand is weak (far from winning), an opponent seems close to winning (few tiles left, called Pongs), or you're leading in points.",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Folding (\u68c4\u7cca): Completely abandon your hand and only discard safe tiles. Break up your melds if needed to find safe discards!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Remember: Not dealing into someone's hand is just as valuable as winning yourself. A draw (\u6d41\u5c40) is better than paying a big hand!",h9,h9)],n5)
