d2=A.a([A.x(h8,"Advanced players use deception! You can mislead opponents about what you're building through strategic discards.",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Example: You're building a Bamboo flush. Discard a Bamboo tile early (like {{s2}}) to make opponents think you DON'T want Bamboo!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,"Early discards carry the strongest signal. If you throw {{s2}} on turn 1, opponents assume Bamboo is safe to discard to you. Perfect trap!",h9,h9),A.x(h8,'Counter-bluffing: If an opponent\'s discards seem "too perfect," they might be bluffing! Experienced players question obvious patterns.',h9,h9)],n5)
